  U.bias = 'Where my own view may be bent: I was trained mostly on English-language text, much of it American, so American framing is my default unless I correct for it. Words carry that framing: the same relationship can be called an “ally,” a “partner,” a “client state” or a “vassal.” There is also a records bias that runs both ways: US crimes are unusually well documented because the US has freedom-of-information laws, a free press and congressional investigations, while closed states hide theirs. That makes the US look worse on paper than secretive powers and also makes US sources the easiest to find. I have tried to hold every power to the same test here: what was done, who decided, who paid, and whether the people affected could say no. Push back wherever you think I failed it.';

